    "owner": "Compromise Checker defaults",
    "reason": "PHP's opcache keeps its JIT code in shared memory, which /proc's maps show as \"/dev/zero (deleted)\". Only the shared-memory kind, only PHP-FPM as installed by the system: a memory-only file, a deleted file or a scratch file mapped into PHP-FPM still shows. Code a script maps the same way (PHP's FFI) looks the same and is let through too."
   },
